_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"New file `Mathlib/AlgebraicTopology/Reedy/Direct.lean`:\n\n`HomotopicalAlgebra.ReedyStructure.ofWellFounded`\n`HomotopicalAlgebra.ReedyStructure.wellFounded`\n`HomotopicalAlgebra.ReedyStructure.eq_id_of_endo`\nan instance `Unique ((identities C).MapFactorizationData ⊤ f)`\n\nA category `C` has a `ReedyStructure (identities C) ⊤ α` (it is *direct*) if and only if the relation « there is a non-identity morphism `X ⟶ Y` » on objects is well-founded. In one direction, the degree is `WellFounded.rank` of that relation, with values in `Ordinal.{u}`, and the factorization axiom holds because `𝟙 ≫ f` is the only factorization whose first factor is an identity. In the other, the relation is a subrelation of the inverse image of `<` under `deg`. A corollary: every endomorphism in a direct category is an identity. Well-foundedness alone already makes the category skeletal and its endomorphisms trivial, so no separate hypotheses are needed.\n\nQuestions for reviewers: whether to introduce a `Prop`-valued class `IsDirect C` (and dually `IsInverse C`) instead of working with `ReedyStructure (identities C) ⊤ α`; whether the `Unique` instance should be a `def`; and whether to add the dual statement for inverse categories via `ReedyStructure.op`.\n\nAI disclosure: the Lean proof was written by an AI model (Claude, Anthropic) under my direction. I have read and checked it and will handle the review. It builds against current master.\n","labels":[{"id":6167106057,"node_id":"LA_kwDOFcwZ1c8AAAABb5aSCQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leanprover-community/mathlib4/labels/new-contributor","name":"new-contributor","description":"This PR was made by a contributor with at most 5 merged PRs. Welcome to the community!","color":"8BBA68","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":9030778799,"node_id":"LA_kwDOFcwZ1c8AAAACGka_rw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leanprover-community/mathlib4/labels/t-algebraic-topology","nam